__pycache__/
*.pyc
venv/
# Track the actual review data (paper.json + per-variant vocab) but not
# the regeneratable/bulky binary output - full-page renders, question
# image crops, and the copied source PDF - which would otherwise make
# this repo grow unboundedly with normal use (git doesn't diff binary
# blobs well, so every reprocess/re-crop would add a whole new copy).
# Diagram crops (src/marks.py) are the one exception: unlike a question
# crop, which Reprocess/a re-run regenerates from the source PDF, a
# diagram only exists because it was manually marked in the Edit-image
# modal - losing it means redrawing the mark, not just re-running
# something, so it's tracked like paper.json rather than treated as
# regeneratable.
output/*
!output/_vocab/
!output/*/
output/*/*
!output/_vocab/*.json
!output/*/paper.json
!output/*/images/
output/*/images/*
!output/*/images/diagrams/
.EasyOCR/
*.egg-info/
dev_ocr_cache/
dev_ocr_cache_hires/
dev_samples/
dev_samples_hires/
data/
flask.log

